// The Windows look's button ring: v3's TcxButton as the native Windows 11 theme draws it at 96 DPI, painted pixel
// for pixel from the captures in docs/ui/looks/ref/windows/dialogs (Search for Card, Filter Card Pool and
// Conditional Formatting draw the crisp ring; the Options, Deck Properties and Deck Legality dialogs show the same
// ring resampled one pixel wider). The visible box of a button whose control rect is W x H is (W - 2) x (H - 1), at
// (1, 1) in the rect. Three rings were captured: rest, default (accent) and disabled. Hover and pressed reuse the
// rest ring with another face (unmeasured). A ring is four 6 x 6 corners, the two-row top and bottom and the
// one-row left and right edges, and the face between; `ring_*_corners` and `ring_*_edges` are generated by a script
// from the captures (a value of 0 is the dialog face, not painted).

